This list is scoped to modules actually IMPORTED by cascade's own packages
across the release GOOS matrix (the go-licenses default: `go list -deps`
transitive closure of compiled code), which is what ships inside the
binaries. github.com/inconshreveable/mousetrap is imported by spf13/cobra
ONLY on GOOS=windows (cobra's windows "double-click" detection) — it does
not appear under darwin/linux go-licenses runs, which is why the union across
all three release GOOSes, not a single-platform run, is required. go.yaml.in/
yaml/v3 and gopkg.in/check.v1 are test-only transitive dependencies of
pelletier/go-toml and are never compiled into any cascade binary on any release
platform. All four remain in go.sum (required to build/test the module
graph); the latter two are intentionally absent from this report, which
documents what actually ships, not the full go.sum.

P1-E02-W1-S02-T2 (R-14.130) added modernc.org/sqlite, the pure-Go (no CGO)
SQLite driver §2/02-TARGET-STRUCTURE mandates, plus its full transitive
closure: modernc.org/libc, modernc.org/mathutil, modernc.org/memory,
golang.org/x/sys (promoted to a direct dependency — providers/sqlite's
flock_linux.go calls golang.org/x/sys/unix.Flock directly per the ticket
text), github.com/dustin/go-humanize, github.com/google/uuid,
github.com/mattn/go-isatty, github.com/ncruces/go-strftime, and
github.com/remyoudompheng/bigfft. Regenerated per this file's own recipe
(`for goos in darwin linux windows; do GOOS=$goos go-licenses csv ./...`)
on 2026-09-02, which surfaced two known go-licenses tool quirks, both
resolved by reading each module's own top-level LICENSE file directly
rather than trusting the tool's file-selection heuristic:
  - modernc.org/libc: go-licenses reports "MIT" against
    LICENSE-3RD-PARTY.md, a bundled note about a *different* embedded
    component, not libc's own license. libc's own top-level LICENSE file
    (verified directly) is BSD-3-Clause, the value recorded above and in
    internal/build/licenses.go's KnownModuleLicenses registry.
  - modernc.org/mathutil: go-licenses reports "Unknown" (a path-matching
    miss in the tool, not a missing license) despite the module carrying a
    top-level LICENSE file. Verified directly: BSD-3-Clause, recorded
    above and in the registry.
internal/build/licenses.go's hand-rolled gate (this repo's actual CI
enforcement point, per its own package doc) is keyed off directly-verified
LICENSE file contents, not off go-licenses' file-selection heuristic, so
these two quirks do not affect the gate's correctness — only this
generated-report recipe's raw output, corrected here.

Per .claude/rules/dependency-rules.md (acamarata dependency policy, applies
project-wide): only MIT, BSD-2/3-Clause, Apache-2.0, ISC, and CC0 licenses are
accepted for cascade's own dependencies. GPL/LGPL/AGPL/SSPL are blocked. All
entries above satisfy that policy.
